  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Genesis",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 43,
    "summary": "Jacob is persuaded to send Benjamin to Egypt—Joseph’s brothers show respect to him—They all eat and drink together.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And the famine was sore in the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:1",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when they had eaten up the corn which they had brought out of Egypt, their father said unto them, Go again, buy us a little food.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:2",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah spake unto him, saying, The man did solemnly protest unto us, saying, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother be with you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "Gen. 44:26 (25–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:3",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou wilt send our brother with us, we will go down and buy thee food:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:4",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "But if thou wilt not send him, we will not go down: for the man said unto us, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother be with you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "Gen. 44:23 (21–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 126
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:5",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Israel said, Wherefore dealt ye so ill with me, as to tell the man whether ye had yet a brother?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:6",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said, The man asked us straitly of our state, and of our kindred, saying, Is your father yet alive? have ye another brother? and we told him according to the tenor of these words: could we certainly know that he would say, Bring your brother down?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 85
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 124
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:7",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah said unto Israel his father, Send the lad with me, and we will arise and go; that we may live, and not die, both we, and thou, and also our little ones.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 140
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:8",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "I will be surety for him; of my hand shalt thou require him: if I bring him not unto thee, and set him before thee, then let me bear the blame for ever:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 142,
            "text": "Gen. 44:32."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 44:32.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 44:32",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 44,
                    "end": 44,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 32,
                        "end": 32
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:9",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "For except we had lingered, surely now we had returned this second time.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:10",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And their father Israel said unto them, If it must be so now, do this; take of the best fruits in the land in your vessels, and carry down the man a present, a little balm, and a little honey, spices, and myrrh, nuts, and almonds:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:11",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And take double money in your hand; and the money that was brought again in the mouth of your sacks, carry it again in your hand; peradventure it was an oversight:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Gen. 42:25 (25, 27, 35)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 109
          },
          {
            "start": 146,
            "end": 149
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:12",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Take also your brother, and arise, go again unto the man:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:13",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And God Almighty give you mercy before the man, that he may send away your other brother, and Benjamin. If I be bereaved of my children, I am bereaved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 136
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:14",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And the men took that present, and they took double money in their hand, and Benjamin; and rose up, and went down to Egypt, and stood before Joseph.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:15",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And when Joseph saw Benjamin with them, he said to the ruler of his house, Bring these men home, and slay, and make ready; for these men shall dine with me at noon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86
          },
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 132
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:16",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And the man did as Joseph bade; and the man brought the men into Joseph’s house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:17",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And the men were afraid, because they were brought into Joseph’s house; and they said, Because of the money that was returned in our sacks at the first time are we brought in; that he may seek occasion against us, and fall upon us, and take us for bondmen, and our asses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:18",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And they came near to the steward of Joseph’s house, and they communed with him at the door of the house,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 43:19",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 43,
        "verse": 19
      },
